<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44157" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sīcundē</span></b> 
		adv.
		si-unde; cf. sicubi, from si-ubi, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>if from anywhere</i> (rare but
			class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicunde potes, erues, qui decem legati Mummio
					fuerint,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 13, 30, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicunde spes aliqua se ostendisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicunde hostis appareat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 51</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicunde discederet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4</span></i>
			.</div>
